Therefore, I would consider this PR a bug fix.  

Plus, I need this fix in order to get my modal that has tabs with hashed routes to work.

@rscotten ah your description in the PR made it seems like something different! 🙏 Can you add integration tests for this change to `test/integration/client-navigation` 👍 

> This allows the developer to pass state into the browser history for hash changes and consume that state in the client app.

Note that this is undesired behavior.

There can be times where a script execution is keeping a body blank by the time `load` event happens. Thus `PerformanceObserver` is used to make this time independent.

a small addition to top of PerformanceObserver can fix this.
// collect already occurred paint timings
performance.getEntriesByType('paint').forEach(onPerfEntry)
// another observer for future paint events
const observer = new PerformanceObserver(list => {
  list.getEntries().forEach(onPerfEntry)
})
observer.observe({ entryTypes: ['paint'] })


Sidenote, after this we can re-enable this test to run in `dev` mode.

@VictorAssis No problem, Is nice to see that you're interested in fixing the example, here's what you can do:

- Have the Layout and auth HOC in the page, and remove `_app`.
- Remove the token from the browser, so in the server you would use [`cookie`](https://github.com/jshttp/cookie) to get the cookie and return the data, and in the client you would to a fetch to an API endpoint that returns the data (use `typeof window === 'undefined'` to know if it's the server or the browser inside `getInitialProps`).

