Commit: 27bbb2b8b4254703d3bfb37fe1dd8aa1f93f437e

@ivawzh The customization to _document.js above serves to keep the auth state in the HTML so that it's accessible after client-side navigation. With `getServerSideProps`, I think you can just eliminate the custom _document.js because data fetching won't happen on the client.

If other static pages (that fetch data on the client-side only) need access to the auth state, they can get the auth state from the Firebase JS SDK.

I haven't thought much about this because I haven't upgraded to Next.js v9.4, so take my suggestions with a grain of salt. Hope this helps!

